# Brand Values

Design First

Every screen should be beautiful before adding features.

---

Experience Before Technology

Technology exists only to support the experience.

---

Speed Matters

Waiting destroys immersion.

Everything should feel immediate.

---

Privacy Matters

The home belongs to the user.

Not to the cloud.

---

Human First

Every interaction should feel natural.

Never robotic.

---

# Tone of Voice

Aura never shouts.

Never uses excessive punctuation.

Never uses emojis.

Never uses technical language unless requested.

Instead Aura speaks clearly.

Examples

Good

Movie Night is ready.

Good Night activated.

Living Room lights are now dimmed.

Apple TV is available.

Avoid

Success!!

Connecting...

Loading...

Initializing API...

Unknown Error 0x00342

---

# Naming Style

Aura uses simple words.

Movie Night

Gaming

Relax

Good Night

Living Room

Bedroom

Kitchen

Never

Execute Automation

Entertainment Profile

Lighting Preset

---

# Logo Philosophy

The logo should be recognizable at 24 pixels.

Simple.

Timeless.

Minimal.

The logo should feel closer to Apple Health than Philips Hue.

No gradients inside the symbol.

No unnecessary detail.

---

# Icon Philosophy

Every icon should use the same visual language.

Rounded.

Simple.

Thin.

Balanced.

Icons must never dominate the interface.

---

# Photography

Aura avoids photography whenever possible.

Instead use

Soft illustrations

Minimal gradients

Ambient lighting

Simple shapes

Photography is reserved only for

Camera previews

TV artwork

Media artwork

---

# Color Philosophy

Aura is not a black interface.

Aura is built around deep midnight tones.

The interface should resemble

A quiet room at night.

Soft ambient lighting.

Not darkness.

---

# Material Philosophy

Aura uses layered surfaces.

Glass.

Depth.

Light.

Motion.

Cards should appear to float.

Not stack.

---

# Typography Philosophy

Typography is the primary visual element.

Large titles.

Generous spacing.

Minimal text.

Never use long paragraphs inside the interface.

One action.

One sentence.

---

# White Space

Whitespace is a feature.

Never fill space simply because it exists.

Every screen should breathe.

---

# Buttons

Buttons should feel physical.

Rounded.

Large.

Easy to hit.

Never tiny.

Never crowded.

---

# Cards

Cards are Aura's primary building block.

Every card contains

Title

Status

Primary Action

Secondary Information

Optional Context Menu

Cards should never exceed one primary purpose.

---

# Motion Philosophy

Motion should communicate

State

Hierarchy

Direction

Feedback

Never decoration.

---

# Haptic Philosophy

Every important action deserves physical confirmation.

Not every tap.

---

# Sound Philosophy

Aura should be nearly silent.

Only meaningful actions receive subtle sound feedback.

---

# Accessibility Philosophy

Beautiful design must never reduce accessibility.

Accessibility is not optional.

It is part of good design.

